  "question": {
    "text": "An amplitude modulated signal is plotted below:\r\n\r\n<img src=\"assets\\qt0078_645d6cd4ca88.png\"><br>\r\n\r\nWhich one of the following best describes the above\r\n\r\nsignal?"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "$\\left(9+\\sin \\left(2.5 \\pi \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right) \\sin \\left(2 \\pi \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{t}\\right) \\mathrm{V}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(1+9 \\sin \\left(2 \\pi \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right) \\sin \\left(2.5 \\pi \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{t}\\right) \\mathrm{V}$",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(9+\\sin \\left(2 \\pi \\times 10^{4} t\\right)\\right) \\sin \\left(2.5 \\pi \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{t}\\right) \\mathrm{V}$",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "$\\left(9+\\sin \\left(4 \\pi \\times 10^{4} t\\right)\\right) \\sin \\left(5 \\pi \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{t}\\right) \\mathrm{V}$",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "C"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "After analysing the graph we may conclude that\r\n\r\n(i) Amplitude varies as $8-10 \\mathrm{~V}$ or $9 \\pm 1$\r\n\r\n(ii) Two time period as\r\n\r\n$100 \\mu$ s (signal wave) $\\& 8 \\mu$ (carrier wave)\r\n\r\nSo, equation of AM signal is\r\n\r\n$\\left[9 \\pm 1 \\sin \\left(\\frac{2 \\pi t}{T_{1}}\\right) \\sin \\left(\\frac{2 \\pi t}{T_{2}}\\right)\\right]$\r\n\r\n$=\\left[9 \\pm \\sin \\left(2 \\pi \\times 10^{4} \\mathrm{t}\\right)\\right] \\sin \\left(2.5 \\pi \\times 10^{5} \\mathrm{t}\\right) \\mathrm{V}$"
  }
